     1,
     "Hi!\r<br>\r<br>I just discovered the optimizing method in rstan. It sounds very useful, but the example stated in the help file does not run and it is not obvious to me how to use it. So, what should the example should have been supposed to be?\r<br>\r<br>Best,\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Sebastian Weber\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CstdeK0wm4cJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2013-03-23T15:39:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: optimizing method?",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Saturday, March 23, 2013 5:46:11 AM UTC-4, Sebastian Weber wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">I just discovered the optimizing method in rstan. It sounds very useful, but the example stated in the help file does not run and it is not obvious to me how to use it. So, what should the example should have been supposed to be? <br></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><br>There were a couple of issues that will get worked out for the next release. Here is a replication from example(glm):<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># example from glm()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>utils</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">anorexia</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MASS&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>anorex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> glm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Postwt</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Prewt</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Treat</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Prewt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                family </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gaussian</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> anorexia</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># extract data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>X </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">anorex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> anorexia$Postwt<br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># write a usual stan model</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<br>data {<br>  int&lt;lower=1&gt; K;<br>  int&lt;lower=K&gt; N;<br>  matrix[N,K]  X;<br>  vector[N]    y;<br>}<br>parameters {<br>  vector[K] beta;<br>  real&lt;lower=0&gt; sigma;<br>}<br>model {<br>  y ~ normal(X * beta, sigma);<br>}<br>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># compile</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model_code</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> X </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> X</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># wrappers for log-likelihood and gradient</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">par</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> par</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>gr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">par</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> grad_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> par</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># optimize</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>opt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">anorex</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log_sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>             method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;BFGS&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> control </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fnscale </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> hessian </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">opt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br> <br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
